 PARITY — web source -> native (features/dashboard/widgets/VehicleHeroCardWidget.tsx)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Data sources : useVehicles, useVehicleState(id), useUnits, useTranslation
                 -> bound through VehicleHeroSource (P1/S8). NO HTTP in the view.
  Layouts      : isCompact = cols<=1 && rows<=1 (status badge + animated battery% + name);
                 else full — name+status header, model/trim subtitle, metric grid
                 (Battery, Range, Cabin; +Outside when isWide = cols>=3); charging banner
                 when is_charging; extra Outside+Ideal row when isTall (rows>=2) && !isWide.
                 -> VehicleHeroLayout.resolve(cols:rows:) (pure, unit-tested).
  SI-floor     : state.ideal_range arrives in METERS -> convertDistanceFromSI(m, unit)=m/factor
                 (km 1000 · mi 1609.344 · ft 0.3048); fmtInt = fmtNumber(_,0) grouped/half-up.
                 state.{inside,outside}_temp arrive in °C -> convertTempFromSI (id / c*9/5+32),
                 rounded int, symbol appended with NO space ("21°C"); charger_power shown as
                 fmtNumber(_,1)+" kW" only when > 0. All ported 1:1 from lib/unitConversion.ts +
                 lib/numberFormat.ts.
  Battery tone : web batteryColor memo — no state -> muted, >50 success, >20 warning, else danger.
  Status badge : status = state.state ?? 'offline'; dot tone mirrors types/fsm/vehicle.ts +
                 theme.ts resolved badgeDot (online=success, driving/updating=info, charging=warning,
                 parked=accent, asleep=neutral, offline=danger; unknown -> capitalized + neutral).
  Empty        : web `vehicle ? … : <EmptyState icon=Car "No vehicle data"/>`
                 -> ContentUnavailableView(car.fill, widget.noVehicle) when no vehicle.
                 A present vehicle with no live state renders the card with `—` cells (web `state?.…`).
  i18n keys from source : widget.vehicleHeroCard ("Vehicle"), widget.noVehicle, widget.battery,
                 widget.range, widget.cabin, widget.outside, widget.charging, widget.idealRange
                 ("Ideal") — ALL present in the strings table; no English literal in the Swift
                 code (everything via VehicleHeroStrings). Status labels via vehicle.state.* keys.
  Registry (registry/vehicle.ts -> "vehicle-hero-card") :
                 id=vehicle-hero-card · category=vehicle · default 2×2 · min 1×2 · max 4×40
                 — pinned by VehicleHeroRegistryTests (executed below).
  States (all render, none hidden) : loading (skeleton) · empty · error (retry) · content,
                 plus freshness chip live/stale/offline + stale auto-refresh + offline/stale banner.
  Telemetry    : view.opened with surface slug "VehicleHeroCardWidget" (P1/S11) — asserted.
  A11y         : VoiceOver labels on the status badge, every metric cell, the refresh/open/retry
                 buttons, and a combined card summary; Dynamic Type fonts; Reduce-Motion honored
                 for the battery numericText transition and the charging-bolt pulse.

